  "findings": [
    "Quest root CTDA24/CTDT20 rows are decoded with stable FormKeys until INDX/QSDT/QSTA; stage/log/target rows remain in the legacy raw sequence and do not enter dialogue eligibility. Native invalid condition lengths fail.",
    "Original 530830 composes quest +50 conditions FIRST, then INFO +18; trailing quest OR groups can cross into INFO. The helper preserves this order, and actual evaluateConditions matches all 14,450 supplied-Boolean results and exact visitation sequences.",
    "The first preregistered INFO-first expectation was falsified at 178 completed cases; Boolean output alone agreed but exact predicate visitation did not. Failure and original hypothesis are retained. The corrected expectation was preregistered and all cases rerun.",
    "Actual ESMStore test resolves reordered masters, preserves scalar bits, global and parameter FormKeys, handles compressed base and winning override records, keeps a same-local-ID record in another plugin separate, and removes tombstoned quests.",
    "Independent raw base Oblivion.esm inventory and typed esmtool output match all 390 quest keys and 719 root conditions, including ordered raw numerical fields; all 3,784 quest condition rows were classified by raw scope. Official M15 inventory/count lock also passes.",
    "Per-file independent raw/typed comparison across all 11 official plugins matches 416 QUST records, 726 root conditions and 4,080 total quest condition rows, with header-master-based quest identities; no winning-override semantic merge is claimed."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "The original composition probe supplies Boolean predicates, null actor/target and a nonnull quest; deleted/SayOnce/history/quest-running behavior and actual predicates are outside that proof. Both x87 control words and callee-saved registers/stack returns are checked.",
    "The content comparison is base Oblivion.esm only; it is not an installed winning-override dialogue claim. Stable master remapping/override/deletion are independently synthetic store tests.",
    "Live Say/SayTo quest condition admission remains pending predicate authority fixes; the canonical root vector and composition helper are prerequisites only. No new compiler or gameplay/audio validation is claimed.",
    "Automatic common-hit speech/resource/condition preparation and publication, INFO history/results, and complete M15S4 normal-input/fresh-process acceptance remain open.",
    "Sanitizer leak detection is disabled. Automated headless engine tests are not rendered/audio or normal-input acceptance."
  ],
